  "preamble": "Complete loss of the uvular ejective. In most Laz dialects (Atina, Vizha, Artasheni, Vitse-Arkabi), Proto-Kartvelian *qʼ disappeared word-initially, presumably via a glottal stop as in neighbouring Megrelian (*qʼ > ʔ). The Khopa-Batumi and Chkhala dialects keep qʼ, so the change is dialectal within Laz. Dialect forms come from Laz dictionaries as reported on Wiktionary, after Klimov (1998) and Fähnrich (2007).",
